1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,260
This deep blue exoplanet rains molten glass sideways at five thousand miles an hour.

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:12,020
HD 189733b looks peaceful, but its atmosphere reaches two thousand degrees Fahrenheit.

3
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:14,830
That extreme heat condenses airborne silicate particles directly into liquid glass.

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:18,860
Pause right now. Guess why this glass falls sideways instead of down.

5
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:24,400
Supersonic winds fly at seven times the speed of sound, whipping rain horizontally.

6
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:28,580
It creates a massive storm of endless, deadly razor-sharp glass blades.

7
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:33,750
The beautiful sapphire color isn't oceans—it is light scattering off glass rain.

8
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:37,240
Standing here would shred you apart before you ever hit the surface.

9
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:40,100
Which explains why...
